  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f(\\theta)=\\left(1+\\sin ^{2} \\theta\\right)\\left(2-\\sin ^{2} \\theta\\right) .$ Then, for all\r\nvalues of $\\theta$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "fekVJ",
      "text": "$f(\\theta)>\\frac{9}{4}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "YF8zb",
      "text": "$f(\\theta)     < 2$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "caAfp",
      "text": "$f(\\theta)>\\frac{11}{4}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "G51Mh",
      "text": "$2 \\leq f(\\theta) \\leq \\frac{9}{4}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\nf(\\theta)=\\left(1+\\sin ^{2} \\theta\\right)\\left(2-\\sin ^{2} \\theta\\right) \\\\\r\n&=2+2 \\sin ^{2} \\theta-\\sin ^{2} \\theta-\\sin ^{4} \\theta \\\\\r\n&=-\\sin ^{4} \\theta+\\sin ^{2} \\theta+2 \\\\\r\n&=-\\left(\\sin ^{4} \\theta-\\sin ^{2} \\theta-2\\right) \\\\\r\n&=-\\left\\{\\sin ^{4} \\theta-\\sin ^{2} \\theta+\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\} \\\\\r\n&=+\\frac{9}{4}-\\left(\\sin ^{2} \\theta-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{2} \\\\\r\n\\because \\quad-1 \\leq \\sin \\theta \\leq 1 \\Rightarrow 0 \\leq \\sin ^{2} \\theta \\leq 1\\\\\r\n\\Rightarrow & 0 \\geq-\\left(\\sin ^{2} \\theta-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{2} \\geq-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\\r\n\\Rightarrow \\quad \\quad-\\frac{1}{2} \\leq \\sin ^{2} \\theta-\\frac{1}{2} \\leq \\frac{1}{2}\\\\\r\n\\Rightarrow \\quad 0 \\leq\\left(\\sin ^{2} \\theta-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{2} \\leq \\frac{1}{4}\r\n\\Rightarrow & \\frac{9}{4} \\geq \\frac{9}{4}-\\left(\\sin ^{2} \\theta-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{2} \\geq \\frac{9}{4}-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\\r\n\\Rightarrow \\quad 2 \\leq f(\\theta) \\leq \\frac{9}{4} & \\quad[\\text { from Eq. }(0)]\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
